            <ArticleTitle>Ruthenium-catalyzed olefinic C-H alkenylation of enol-carbamates: highly stereo-selective synthesis of (Z,Z) and (Z,E)-butadienes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12926-12929</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07777g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cross-coupling reactions of enol carbamates with alkynes or alkenes are reported, using an inexpensive ruthenium catalyst. With the assistance of the directing group OCONMe2, the protocols provide mild, stereo-selective and efficient routes for the preparation of valuable (Z,Z) and (Z,E)-butadiene skeletons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
